# Learning Log

During this project we learned several important software engineering practices.

Testing
We learned how to use pytest to create automated unit tests. Testing helped us identify logic issues, particularly with handling the scoring algorithm.

Version Control
Using Git allowed us to collaborate effectively. Branching ensured that each developer could work independently without breaking the main codebase.

Prompt Engineering
AI tools were used to assist with development. However, prompts needed to be carefully refined to produce useful outputs.

Algorithm Design
The scoring algorithm required careful handling of duplicates. for example implementing a two-pass system ensured that exact matches were processed before partial matches.

Reflection
This project demonstrated the importance of testing, clear requirements, and structured development when building reliable software.